## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Component Testing Requirements

### ALL Components MUST Include data-testid Attributes

**MANDATORY:** Every component you create MUST include `data-testid` attributes for E2E testing.

### Required Elements

When creating ANY component (page, form, UI control, etc.):

✅ **MUST add data-testid to:**
- Container/root element
- All buttons
- All form inputs (text, number, select, checkbox, radio)
- All links
- All interactive elements
- Success/error message containers
- Calculated value displays
- List containers and list items

### Naming Convention

```
data-testid="{module}-{component}-{element}-{action}"
```

**Rules:**
- Use kebab-case (lowercase-with-dashes)
- Include module prefix (`explore`, `build`, `report`)
- Be descriptive but concise
- Include action for buttons (`save-button`, `delete-button`)

### ✅ CORRECT Example with data-testid

```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-property-form',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [CommonModule, ReactiveFormsModule],
  template: `
    <form
      [formGroup]="form"
      (ngSubmit)="onSubmit()"
      class="card p-6 space-y-6"
      data-testid="property-form">

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Create Property</h2>

      @if (errorMessage()) {
        <div
          class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-800"
          data-testid="property-form-error-message">
          {{ errorMessage() }}
        </div>
      }

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div>
          <label for="address" class="label">Address</label>
          <input
            type="text"
            id="address"
            formControlName="address"
            class="input"
            data-testid="property-form-address-input"
          />
        </div>

        <div>
          <label for="city" class="label">City</label>
          <input
            type="text"
            id="city"
            formControlName="city"
            class="input"
            data-testid="property-form-city-input"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex justify-end gap-4">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="btn-secondary"
          data-testid="property-form-cancel-button">
          Cancel
        </button>

        <button
          type="submit"
          class="btn-primary"
          [disabled]="isPending() || form.invalid"
          data-testid="property-form-submit-button">
          {{ isPending() ? 'Creating...' : 'Create Property' }}
        </button>
      </div>

      @if (successMessage()) {
        <div
          class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-green-50 text-green-800"
          data-testid="property-form-success-message">
          {{ successMessage() }}
        </div>
      }
    </form>
  `
})
```

### Dynamic data-testid for Lists

Use `[attr.data-testid]` for dynamic elements:

```typescript
@Component({
  template: `
    <div data-testid="property-list">
      @for (property of properties(); track property.id) {
        <div [attr.data-testid]="'property-item-' + property.id">
          <h3>{{ property.address }}</h3>
          <button
            [attr.data-testid]="'property-edit-button-' + property.id"
            (click)="edit(property)">
            Edit
          </button>
        </div>
      }
    </div>
  `
})
```

