## Modern Template Syntax (v17+)

### ✅ CORRECT: Built-in control flow (@if, @for, @switch)

```html
<!-- @if directive -->
@if (isLoading()) {
  <div class="spinner">Loading...</div>
} @else if (error()) {
  <div class="alert-error">{{ error() }}</div>
} @else {
  <div class="content">{{ properties().length }} properties</div>
}

<!-- @for directive with track -->
@for (property of properties(); track property.id) {
  <div class="card p-6">
    <h3>{{ property.address }}</h3>
    <p>{{ property.city }}, {{ property.state }}</p>

    @if (property.pumpCount > 16) {
      <span class="badge-promo">Large Station</span>
    }
  </div>
} @empty {
  <p class="text-text-secondary">No properties found</p>
}

<!-- @switch directive -->
@switch (property.status) {
  @case ('active') {
    <span class="badge-tag bg-green-100 text-green-800">Active</span>
  }
  @case ('pending') {
    <span class="badge-tag bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-800">Pending</span>
  }
  @case ('inactive') {
    <span class="badge-tag bg-gray-100 text-gray-800">Inactive</span>
  }
  @default {
    <span class="badge-tag">Unknown</span>
  }
}
```

### ❌ WRONG: Old structural directives

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD: Using *ngIf (old syntax, still works but not preferred) -->
<div *ngIf="isLoading(); else content">
  <div class="spinner">Loading...</div>
</div>
<ng-template #content>
  <div>Content</div>
</ng-template>

<!-- ❌ BAD: Using *ngFor without trackBy -->
